WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:05.279
Euron Greyjoy:When Aegon finally saw the monstrous
castle, he asked for parley.

00:00:05.279 --> 00:00:07.959
Harren granted it.

00:00:07.959 --> 00:00:12.230
Valyria had been the greatest empire the world
had ever seen.

00:00:12.230 --> 00:00:15.690
Harren wanted to piss on its ashes.

00:00:15.690 --> 00:00:21.980
Viserys Targaryen: (as Aegon) "Yield now,
and you may remain Lord of the Iron Islands.

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:26.849
Yield now, and your sons will live to rule
after you.

00:00:26.849 --> 00:00:30.140
You see my army outside your walls.

00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:31.390
You see my dragons."

00:00:31.390 --> 00:00:36.410
Euron: (as Harren) "What is outside my walls
is of no concern.

00:00:36.410 --> 00:00:38.540
Those walls are strong and thick."

00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:40.650
Viserys: (as Aegon) "Dragons fly."

00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:44.980
Euron: (as Harren) "But stone doesn't burn."

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:49.390
Viserys: (as Aegon) "When the sun sets, your
line shall end."

00:00:49.390 --> 00:00:54.530
Euron: Harren spat and returned to his castle.

00:00:54.530 --> 00:00:59.690
Once inside, he promised lands, riches, and
Tully's daughters to whoever could bring down

00:00:59.690 --> 00:01:02.130
Aegon or his dragon.

00:01:02.130 --> 00:01:09.020
As the sun sank below the horizon, all Harren's
men patrolled the battlements, hearing wings

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:12.000
in every gust of wind.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:16.799
But the moon rose and sank, and no dragon
appeared.

00:01:16.799 --> 00:01:22.490
Viserys: While the ironborn were ringing the
battlements, Aegon drove his dragon Balerion

00:01:22.490 --> 00:01:26.969
higher and higher in the night sky, so that
even the great castle of Harrenhal looked

00:01:26.969 --> 00:01:28.630
like an anthill below them.

00:01:28.630 --> 00:01:34.130
Then they plunged straight into the castle,
well inside the guarded walls.

00:01:34.130 --> 00:01:38.130
The five towers of Harrenhal reached towards
Aegon like a hand.

00:01:38.130 --> 00:01:42.079
Balerion opened his mouth and bathed all the
fingers in flame.

00:01:42.079 --> 00:01:45.119
Euron: Harren was right.

00:01:45.119 --> 00:01:51.659
Stone doesn't burn, but men do, even when
they're ironborn.

00:01:51.659 --> 00:01:58.310
The dragon blasted my ancestors into ash that
choked the survivors when they screamed.

00:01:58.310 --> 00:02:02.249
Harren's soldiers leapt from the battlements
and died.

00:02:02.249 --> 00:02:05.180
They huddled against the walls and died.

00:02:05.180 --> 00:02:08.629
They fled across the yard and died.

00:02:08.629 --> 00:02:16.299
Harren and his sons took shelter inside the
castle.

00:02:16.299 --> 00:02:22.890
The stone didn't burn, but as Balerion blasted
it with fire, it glowed white-hot.

00:02:22.890 --> 00:02:30.200
The world's greatest castle became the world's
greatest oven, baking the last of House Hoare

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:31.480
within it.

00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:37.379
Viserys: Outside the castle walls, the towers
of Harrenhal glowed red against the night

00:02:37.379 --> 00:02:42.790
and began to twist and melt like five huge
candles, with liquid stone trickling down

00:02:42.790 --> 00:02:45.549
their sides like wax.

00:02:45.549 --> 00:02:48.650
The next morning, Aegon forged a new Riverlands.

00:02:48.650 --> 00:02:54.300
He named the rebel Edmyn Tully as his Lord
Paramount of the Trident and had the other

00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:57.439
riverlords swear him fealty as their new liege.

00:02:57.439 --> 00:03:01.989
For centuries, House Hoare had terrorized
the Riverlands.

00:03:01.989 --> 00:03:08.060
Under House Tully, the Riverlands would, at
last, return to peace and prosperity.

00:03:08.060 --> 00:03:13.069
After the castle cooled enough to allow men
inside, Aegon ventured into the ruin he had

00:03:13.069 --> 00:03:14.890
made of Harrenhal.

00:03:14.890 --> 00:03:21.170
He saw the ashen bodies, the scorched stone,
and the mangled and melted swords of his former

00:03:21.170 --> 00:03:22.390
enemies.

00:03:22.390 --> 00:03:27.650
To his men's confusion, he ordered these useless
swords collected and sent to his Aegonfort.

00:03:27.650 --> 00:03:32.939
Theon Greyjoy: When Aegon and his dragons
burned Harren the Black and all his sons at

00:03:32.939 --> 00:03:36.739
Harrenhal, the days when men feared the sight
of our longships were over.

00:03:36.739 --> 00:03:39.810
Aegon would not permit marauders and raiders
in his Seven Kingdoms.

00:03:39.810 --> 00:03:44.439
With Harren died our empire and the Old Way
that forged it.

00:03:44.439 --> 00:03:48.230
But what is dead may never die.

00:03:48.230 --> 00:03:52.849
Six years after Robert Baratheon won his crown,
my father, Balon Greyjoy, sought to restore

00:03:52.849 --> 00:03:54.930
our ancient rights.

00:03:54.930 --> 00:03:59.650
He declared the Iron Islands independent,
and himself its king and sent the Iron Fleet

00:03:59.650 --> 00:04:04.290
in a daring raid on Lannisport where they
burned the Lannister ships at anchor, making

00:04:04.290 --> 00:04:06.519
us unchallenged in the Sunset Sea.

00:04:06.519 --> 00:04:09.530
This was the seed of our undoing.

00:04:09.530 --> 00:04:15.170
My eldest brother, Rodrik, led a frontal assault
on Seagard, a town built to protect the mainland

00:04:15.170 --> 00:04:16.370
from us.

00:04:16.370 --> 00:04:20.690
After ferocious fighting beneath the city
walls, he was slain by Lord Jason Mallister,

00:04:20.690 --> 00:04:21.690
and his men defeated.

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:26.530
By this time, Stannis Baratheon had brought
Robert's fleet around Westeros and somehow

00:04:26.530 --> 00:04:30.650
managed to trap the Iron Fleet at Fair Isle,
smashing it.

00:04:30.650 --> 00:04:36.490
Robert's victory was now all but assured,
yet we made him bleed for each island.

00:04:36.490 --> 00:04:41.090
Stannis Baratheon captured Great Wyk, the
largest of the Iron Islands, and Ser Barristan

00:04:41.090 --> 00:04:44.020
Selmy himself subdued Old Wyk.

00:04:44.020 --> 00:04:50.310
Robert and Lord Eddard Stark led the main
assault against the island of Pyke.

00:04:50.310 --> 00:04:54.470
They razed the town of Lordsport to the ground
before Robert turned his full fury on our

00:04:54.470 --> 00:04:57.050
family's stronghold.

00:04:57.050 --> 00:05:01.990
When they breached the walls, the first through
was Thoros of Myr with his ridiculous flaming

00:05:01.990 --> 00:05:07.680
sword, followed by every minor lord of Westeros
hungering for glory.

00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:12.560
My other brother, Maron, was killed when the
siege engines brought down a tower on his

00:05:12.560 --> 00:05:13.560
head.

00:05:13.560 --> 00:05:18.970
I was now my father's only living son and
heir to the Iron Islands.

00:05:18.970 --> 00:05:24.720
When my father saw that his cause was lost,
he wisely conceded defeat to Robert, who otherwise

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:28.850
would have pulled down our castle stone by
stone with us in it.

00:05:28.850 --> 00:05:33.520
As my father said to me then, "No man has
ever died from bending his knee.

00:05:33.520 --> 00:05:37.000
He who kneels may rise again, blade in hand.

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:41.250
He who'll not kneel stays dead, stiff legs
and all."

00:05:41.250 --> 00:05:45.819
As it stands, Robert allowed my father to
keep his lands and title as Lord of the Iron

00:05:45.819 --> 00:05:51.770
Islands, King of Salt and Rock, Son of the
Sea Wind, Lord Reaper of Pyke.

00:05:51.770 --> 00:05:53.440
For a price.

00:05:53.440 --> 00:05:57.190
His last son and heir shipped off to Winterfell
as an "honored guest."

00:05:57.190 --> 00:06:01.849
I would eat at the Starks' table and play
with the Stark children.

00:06:01.849 --> 00:06:08.389
And if my father rebelled again, Lord Eddard
Stark would take his sword and cut off my

00:06:08.389 --> 00:06:09.680
head.

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:12.680
It would be his duty.

00:06:12.680 --> 00:06:18.620
Stannis Baratheon: Though Robert had risked
all our lives to win it, the Iron Throne bored

00:06:18.620 --> 00:06:19.620
him.

00:06:19.620 --> 00:06:22.630
He cared little for justice and less for rule.

00:06:22.630 --> 00:06:26.900
If it weren't women or wineskin, he had no
use for it.

00:06:26.900 --> 00:06:32.440
Without the stalwart Jon Arryn as Hand of
the King, the challenge to Robert's crown

00:06:32.440 --> 00:06:35.610
would have come much earlier than it did.

00:06:35.610 --> 00:06:38.830
The Iron Islands have never lacked for treachery.

00:06:38.830 --> 00:06:45.140
They respect only strength, and honor is as
foreign to them as the Seven.

00:06:45.140 --> 00:06:52.569
After six years, their ruler, Lord Balon Greyjoy,
wagered that King Robert had not won the support

00:06:52.569 --> 00:06:58.639
of the Great Houses of Westeros, many of whom
still named him "Usurper."

00:06:58.639 --> 00:07:05.620
Lord Balon declared the Iron Islands independent
and sent his Iron Fleet to Lannisport.

00:07:05.620 --> 00:07:12.110
Lord Tywin Lannister was careless, and the
ironborn burnt his ships at anchor.

00:07:12.110 --> 00:07:16.380
Lord Balon and his reavers controlled the
Sunset Sea.

00:07:16.380 --> 00:07:22.660
Robert then ordered me to succeed where his
father-in-law, Lord Tywin, had failed.

00:07:22.660 --> 00:07:26.490
Beneath Robert's fury, I sensed relief.

00:07:26.490 --> 00:07:28.340
War, he could understand.

00:07:28.340 --> 00:07:32.830
He would smash Lord Balon as he had Rhaegar.

00:07:32.830 --> 00:07:37.990
I raised Robert's fleet and sailed around
Westeros to the Iron Islands.

00:07:37.990 --> 00:07:43.000
I set a trap for the Iron Fleet off Fair Isle.

00:07:43.000 --> 00:07:49.530
As sailors and warriors, the ironborn are
unparalleled, but they are not soldiers.

00:07:49.530 --> 00:07:54.159
They have no discipline, no strategy, no unity.

00:07:54.159 --> 00:07:59.259
In a battle, each man fights only for his
own glory, and their longships are built for

00:07:59.259 --> 00:08:02.710
lightning strikes and shore raids.

00:08:02.710 --> 00:08:08.710
When the captains rushed in, I smashed their
longships with our larger war galleys.

00:08:08.710 --> 00:08:12.189
The strength of the ironborn is in their ships.

00:08:12.189 --> 00:08:17.330
With the Iron Fleet broken, I had assured
Robert's victory.

00:08:17.330 --> 00:08:23.560
He could now transport troops and siege weapons
to invade the Iron Islands, and contrary to

00:08:23.560 --> 00:08:26.770
Balon's hopes, Robert had plenty of both.

00:08:26.770 --> 00:08:31.560
I've never seen such allegiances Robert could
inspire in war.

00:08:31.560 --> 00:08:35.500
Enemies who tried to kill him one day would
be drinking with him the next under their

00:08:35.500 --> 00:08:37.290
own fallen banners.

00:08:37.290 --> 00:08:43.010
In rebelling against the Iron Throne, Lord
Balon did more than Robert ever could to cement

00:08:43.010 --> 00:08:44.670
his rule.

00:08:44.670 --> 00:08:51.200
When Robert came to the Iron Islands, he brought
with him the full power of Westeros.

00:08:51.200 --> 00:08:57.330
Ser Barristan Selmy of the Kingsguard led
the assault on Old Wyk while I subdued Great

00:08:57.330 --> 00:08:59.930
Wyk, the largest of the Iron Islands.

00:08:59.930 --> 00:09:07.260
But Robert saved the seat of House Greyjoy,
Pyke, for himself and Lord Eddard.

00:09:07.260 --> 00:09:12.130
Robert would later boast of the battle's bloodiness
and how he could have torn down the island

00:09:12.130 --> 00:09:15.339
into the waves if Lord Balon had not bent
the knee.

00:09:15.339 --> 00:09:22.650
But if I had led the assault, Balon's neck
would have bent under a sword.

00:09:22.650 --> 00:09:26.810
Because I do not forget or pardon.

00:09:26.810 --> 00:09:28.820
His time will come.

00:09:28.820 --> 00:09:30.220
All their times will come.

00:09:30.220 --> 00:09:35.709
Yara Greyjoy: The Seven are gods of weakness
and defeat, pretty chains that the First Men

00:09:35.709 --> 00:09:41.560
kindly put on after the Andals crushed them,
except in the Iron Islands.

00:09:41.560 --> 00:09:47.180
Since the Dawn Age, the Ironborn have followed
the Drowned God, who plucked fire from the

00:09:47.180 --> 00:09:53.310
sea and made us to reave and sack and carve
our names in blood and song.

00:09:53.310 --> 00:09:58.300
When the Andals landed on the Iron Islands,
they found a god who was Father, Warrior,

00:09:58.300 --> 00:10:04.089
and Stranger; who took Mother, Maiden, and
Crone when he would; and held the Smith in

00:10:04.089 --> 00:10:05.389
thrall.

00:10:05.389 --> 00:10:10.959
His priests are Drowned Men, who are clothed
and armed by the sea itself.

00:10:10.959 --> 00:10:17.190
They consecrate us to the Drowned God through
our most sacred rite, the Drowning, and ask

00:10:17.190 --> 00:10:22.620
the God to raise them from the sea as he was,
harder and stronger.

00:10:22.620 --> 00:10:27.740
The ironborn do not fear the bloodiest battle
or the roughest waves, for the Drowned God

00:10:27.740 --> 00:10:31.440
taught us long ago that what is dead may never
die.

00:10:31.440 --> 00:10:36.110
When an Ironborn falls, we say that the Drowned
God needed a strong oarsman and took him below

00:10:36.110 --> 00:10:40.940
to feast in the God's watery halls, attended
by mermaids.

00:10:40.940 --> 00:10:44.649
But even in death, an ironborn is a warrior.

00:10:44.649 --> 00:10:49.950
We fight against the Storm God, who holds
a castle in the clouds and sends the winds

00:10:49.950 --> 00:10:53.940
to lure the ironborn off course or wreck their
ships.

00:10:53.940 --> 00:10:58.441
It's said my legendary ancestor, the Grey
King, waged war against upon the Storm God

00:10:58.441 --> 00:11:00.600
for a thousand years.

00:11:00.600 --> 00:11:05.709
With the Drowned God's help, he slew the great
Sea Dragon Nagga and used her bones for his

00:11:05.709 --> 00:11:07.180
hall.

00:11:07.180 --> 00:11:12.380
After his death, the Storm God tried to wash
away any memory of this terrible foe, but

00:11:12.380 --> 00:11:16.290
his songs fill our halls to this day.

00:11:16.290 --> 00:11:22.180
It was the Storm God who first blew the Andals
to the Iron Islands; to subdue us and turn

00:11:22.180 --> 00:11:24.060
us from our faith.

00:11:24.060 --> 00:11:29.630
True, they conquered and killed our king;
but in time, they forsook their septs for

00:11:29.630 --> 00:11:34.360
the shore and their fat Septons for the Drowned
Men.

00:11:34.360 --> 00:11:40.410
The Andals came to us conquerors; in the end,
they drowned.

00:11:40.410 --> 00:11:47.630
The ironborn are of the sea, as our God made
us, and given to it as our God taught us.

00:11:47.630 --> 00:11:50.820
We do not fear the Storm God's winds or his
waves.

00:11:50.820 --> 00:11:54.360
But you should, for they bring us to you.

